    pluto: add ML-DSA (FIPS 204) post-quantum authentication support

    Add ML-DSA digital signature support for IKEv2 authentication as
    specified in draft-ietf-ipsecme-ikev2-pqc-auth. This implements
    ML-DSA-44, ML-DSA-65, and ML-DSA-87 parameter sets using NSS as
    the crypto backend.

    Changes include:
    - ASN.1 OID definitions for ML-DSA-44/65/87 identity blobs
    - pubkey_type_mldsa and pubkey_signer_digsig_mldsa_{44,65,87}
    - IKEv2 Digital Signature method support with automatic parameter
      set selection based on private key signature length
    - USE_MLDSA feature flag in mk/config.mk (default: false)
    - authby=mldsa connection configuration keyword
    - Hash signature buffer enlarged to accommodate ML-DSA-87 (4627 bytes)
    - RC_LOG logging of the negotiated hash algorithm and signature/PQC
      algorithm (RSASSA-PSS, ECDSA, EDDSA, ML-DSA-44/65/87) for both
      signing and verifying the IKEv2 AUTH payload, so test consoles
      show what was actually negotiated

    Select the ML-DSA signer by reading the actual FIPS 204 parameter set
    off the public key (SECKEYPublicKey.u.mldsa.paramSet) instead of
    inferring it from the private key's maximum signature length; and set
    pkc->keyid for ML-DSA keys the same way ECDSA/EDDSA do (via
    keyblob_to_keyid() over the ckaid), fixing an EXPECTATION FAILED hit
    on every connection load with an ML-DSA cert.

